Package: convertible-helper
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0, udev, ${misc:Depends}
Breaks: panasonic-cf19-support (<< 1.4.0)
Recommends: gnome-session-bin | xfce4-session | plasma-workspace
Description: tablet-mode and tablet-button helper for convertible laptops
 A small user service for convertible laptops that uses no desktop-shell
 code: it resets the screen to normal orientation when the laptop leaves tablet
 mode (otherwise GNOME can leave it turned), and it handles the rotation and
 "security" buttons of the Panasonic Toughbook CF-19 in any shell state.
 .
 It reads the tablet-mode switch and button events from the input devices
 (made readable for the seat's user by a udev rule) and rotates the built-in
 display through mutter's DisplayConfig D-Bus interface.
